    "result_text": "The full suite is green (the repo has a single test class). Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\n`POST /api/owners` now assigns a server-side `customerCode` formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` \u2014 the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` plus a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count.\n\n**Changes (kept as small, cohesive units to minimize structural impact):**\n\n1. **New function class** `AssignCustomerCode.java` \u2014 a fresh single-method class (no surrounding context to hold). It reads the built `Owner` via `@Val`, computes `LAST3` from `lastName`, and derives the sequence from `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1`, mutating the entity in place so the existing `SaveOwner` persists it.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `customerCode` step between `build` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance as the surrounding steps.\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field with a plain getter/setter (each CC 1). MapStruct auto-maps it onto the response DTO by name, exactly as it does for `initials`/`displayName`.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` (readOnly) to the `Owner` response schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it out through `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** + **`data.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column (the test DB uses `ddl-auto=none`, matching the repo's precedent of only maintaining the hsqldb schema for `registration_date`) and a trailing `NULL` for the seed rows.\n\nThe acceptance test's global-sequence check (`cb == ca + 1`) holds because the count is read before this owner is saved, so each successive create sees one more existing owner.",
